{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:58:51.944Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"12e7f77380f45f7a248cc0dc366f08688886ddb56640ca20c740cd9962124b2b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, I found three ticket numbers for Marrow Fieldworks. I'm sure about two of them and fairly sure about the third.\n\n*Moss's notes* (teams/team-central/digests/2026-01-02-central-handoffs.md, the 2 Jan 2026 handoff digest):\n• *#4409*: a timeout that keeps coming back on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it before the 5 Jan handoff.\n• *#4412*: a small glitch in the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots. Hollis flagged this one at the same time.\nThat note names Marrow Fieldworks and calls it \"Pree's dealer account.\"\n\n*#central-random* (13 Oct, 09:27, your own message):\n• *#8841*: West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk, at the Plains depots. Hollis's question just before it calls this \"Tobias's dealer account\" but never says \"Marrow Fieldworks.\" I'm assuming it's the same account because the handoff note calls Marrow Fieldworks the dealer account, but please check before the call.\n\nTwo things that look similar but aren't Fieldworks:\n• *FR-882*, in the same Moss digest, is a feature request from *Marrow Agrisupply*, which is a different account.\n• *#88412* is Tansleigh Packaging, from #central-team. I mention it only because it's easy to mix up with #8841.\n\nMoss's other Central note, the cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers. There's also no account folder for Marrow Fieldworks in the files I can see, so I couldn't check these against the CRM or the ticket records."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:58:57.669Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"214b215ec9b40b830be55fc355d2be8fe1fb107d2b9ff4a312ea545d312a29a4","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I sent Tobias the list in our DM. It has three ticket numbers for Marrow Fieldworks: two are certain and one he should check before the call.\n\n- **#4409** (from Moss's handoff note dated 2 Jan 2026): a timeout that keeps coming back on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard. The note names Marrow Fieldworks directly.\n- **#4412** (same note): a small glitch in the driver text-message prompt when combine trailers are parked on unpaved overflow lots.\n- **#8841** (from Tobias's own message in #central-random on 13 Oct): West yard Door 2 is double-booking when flatbeds check in early. That thread only says \"Tobias's dealer account\" and never names Marrow Fieldworks. I think it's the same account because the handoff note calls Fieldworks \"the dealer account,\" and I told him to confirm that.\n\nI also warned him about two numbers that look related but aren't:\n- **FR-882** is a feature request from Marrow Agrisupply, a different account.\n- **#88412** belongs to Tansleigh Packaging and is easy to confuse with #8841.\n\nI couldn't check any of these against the CRM or the ticket records because there's no Marrow Fieldworks account folder in the files I can see. Everything I used came from a public file and a channel Tobias is in, so nothing needed approval."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
